  {
    "_": "WHERE A SECOND LOCALE GOES (TASK-L162). One key per language code, each holding the same namespaces as the two nodes above: {\"fr\": {\"home\": {\"headline\": \"...\"}}}. English is the BASE and is never a key here — a key you do not translate renders English, on its own, for the kit and for the graph alike. Adding a code here is the whole of adding a locale: nothing else in the graph names a language.",
    "_shipped": "This template ships ONE locale, English. This node is empty of locales on purpose — it is a seam, not an omission. The switch that reads it has been driven against a throwaway second locale and works; no translation has been written or reviewed."
  }
